   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = w \\) and \\( dv = e^{4 w}\\,dw \\), so \\( du = dw \\) and \\( v = \\frac{e^{4 w}}{4} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99056",
         "rule_named": "choice of u and dv"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Integration by parts gives \\( \\frac{w e^{4 w}}{4} - \\int \\frac{e^{4 w}}{4}\\,dw \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99057",
         "rule_named": "integration by parts"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "So the integral is \\( \\left[\\frac{w e^{4 w}}{4} - \\frac{e^{4 w}}{16}\\right]_{0}^{2} = \\frac{1}{16} + \\frac{7 e^{8}}{16} \\).",
